      "@id": "kt:claude-shannon",
      "@type": "kto:Person",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Claude Shannon",
      "skos:definition": "American mathematician and engineer (1916–2001), founder of information theory, whose 1950 paper \"Programming a Computer for Playing Chess\" set out the minimax search, evaluation function and Type A / Type B strategies on which chess programs have been built ever since.",
