      "@id": "kt:castling",
      "@type": "kto:Rule",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Castling",
      "skos:definition": "The special move in which a player moves the king two squares along the first rank towards an unmoved rook and places that rook on the square the king crossed; it counts as a single king move and is allowed only under conditions set out in the FIDE Laws of Chess.",
